mothershipOS: a playback request's payload is everything readable after the transfer header. virtio-queue's
`Reader::available_bytes()` already counts only what is left to read, so subtracting `bytes_read()` (the 4-byte
header) a second time cut the last frame of every guest period: with S16 stereo, one frame in 1024 was lost
(a phase jump 47 times a second, heard as roughness on everything a VM plays).

